<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Registers the "alternative view" key as a real game input action, so it shows up
    in Options -> Key Bindings and can be remapped like any other binding.

    EventType="All" is what makes hold-to-view possible: the action then reports
    START when the key goes down and FINISH when it comes back up, instead of a
    single press. The game uses the same trick for "keyboard-camera-modifier".

    Default is KEY_TAB, a regular key rather than a modifier, and free in both the base
    game and every installed mod.

    Bare modifiers work as an XML default but NOT as a rebinding: the engine's gesture
    recorder (Input.beginRecordingGestures) treats a modifier as the start of a
    combination, so a player who rebinds away from Shift can never record plain Shift
    again - only a full reset of every binding brings it back. KEY_CONTROL went one step
    further and showed up as "unassigned" outright. A regular key keeps the binding
    reversible, which matters more here than the key itself.

    IMPORTANT: these tables live in the FRONTEND/config database, not the gameplay one.
    This file must be loaded from a scope="shell" action group only. Loading it in a
    scope="game" group fails with 'no such table: InputActions' and rolls back that
    group's entire UpdateDatabase action.

    <Replace> rather than <Row>, matching how other mods do it: it is idempotent, so
    re-applying the mod cannot fail on an existing row.
-->
<Database>
    <InputActions>
        <Replace ActionId="najane-alternative-view"
                 DeviceType="Keyboard"
                 Name="LOC_INPUT_NAJANE_ALTERNATIVE_VIEW"
                 Description="LOC_INPUT_NAJANE_ALTERNATIVE_VIEW_HELP"
                 EventType="All" />
    </InputActions>
    <InputActionDefaultGestures>
        <Replace ActionId="najane-alternative-view" Index="0"
                 GestureType="KBMouse" GestureData="KEY_TAB" />
    </InputActionDefaultGestures>
    <InputContextConstraints>
        <Replace ActionId="najane-alternative-view" ContextId="World" />
        <Replace ActionId="najane-alternative-view" ContextId="Unit" />
    </InputContextConstraints>
</Database>
